## Results and Discussion
## rystal Structures and Synergetic Effect Analyses
To introduce aromatic D-A interactions into the coordination assembly, coronene is directly added into the tpt-involved reaction system. Solvothermal reaction of $Z n(N O_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6H_{2}O,$ 1,4-ndc, tpt, and coronene in DMAc at $120^{\circ}\mathsf C$ for 3 days affords red hombus crystals of coronene-MOF-1. Single crystal X-ray diffraction analysis reveals that it crystallizes in the trigonal system with the $_{R-3m}$ space group. The asymmetric unit comprises one $Z n^{2+}$ with $_{1/2}$ occupancy, half $1,4-n\mathsf{d c}^{2-}$ , one sixth tpt, and one $s^{\prime}(t h$ coronene. The $Z n^{2+}$ centre has a square pyramidal coordination geometry, in which four carboxylic oxygen atoms of different 1,4-ndc2− constitute the equatorial plane and one pyridyl itrogen atom of tpt occupies the axial position. Two crystallographically equivalent $\dot{Z}n^{2+}$ are bridged by four uniform arboxylic groups and generate the typical $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ paddle wheel unit. On account of the steric hindrance, two carboxylic $\scriptstyle\mathbf{\sigma}\sim\mathbf{-r}\mathbf{\sigma}\Lambda$ twist off the naphthyl plane reversely to give an almost vertical conformation with the dihedral angel of $87.89^{\circ}$ (Figure S1). The $1,4-n\mathsf{d}\mathsf{c}^{2-}$ caused the reticulation of the $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ at an appropriate angle to each other and ultimately into an NbO network (Figure 1a,b). Due to the specific orientation of the ,4-ndc2− and unprecise perpendicularity of two carboxylic groups, the NbO network is not in the highest symmetrical cubic system but in the trigonal system. Six $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ and six naphthyl linkers re connected alternatively to define an open nano-channel (Figure S2). Then, these channels are intercepted regularly by tpt modules through coordination with $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ units and lead to the trigonal anti-prismatic $[\mathsf{Z n}_{12}(1,4\mathsf{-n d c})_{6}(\mathsf{t p t})_{2}]$ coordination cages (Figure S3). Therefore, coronene-MOF-1 can be simplified as an unusual 2-donal $^{3,6-c}$ loh1 network, considering tpt and $[z n_{2}(00)_{4}]$ as 3- and 6-connected nodes (Figure S4).
Further analysis indicates that the internal space of trigonal anti-prisms is fully occupied by dimeric coronene and generates the unique (coronene $\mathsf{\Gamma})_{2}@[\mathsf{Z n}_{12}(1,4\mathsf{-n d c})_{6}(\mathsf{t p t})_{2}]$ supramolecular building blocks (SBBs), which is composed of tetrameric tpt-coronene-coronene-tpt stacks and the surrounding 1,4-ndc-Zn coordination array (Figure 1c-f, and S5). The distances between tpt and coronene as well as coronene dimer are 3.317 and 3.504 Å (Table 1), respectively, indicating strong supramolecular interactions between the moieties (Figure S8).[10c] The embedded coronene dimer and related D-A as well as the $\pi{-}\pi$ interactions make coronene-MOF-1 a complicated system. Therefore, simplifying the whole (coronene) $\mathsf{\Lambda}_{2}@[2\mathsf{n}_{12}(1,4\mathsf{-n d c})_{6}(\mathsf{t p t})_{2}]$ SBB as node is a more logical route to understand this structure. In this view, coronene-MOF-1 can be regarded as a simple 6-c pcu net, in which each solid trigonal anti-prism node interacts with six adjacent such notes through sharing the $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ vertices (Figure 1g,h, and S6). In spite of the coronene implantation, coronene-MOF-1 still has a solvent-accessible void volume of $43.6\%$ (probe radius $1.8\mathring{\mathsf{A}})$ after removing the lattice solvents, as calculated by PLATON.[13]
A careful analysis of this structure reveals that tpt modules adopt an unusual bending configuration to cater for the coordination with three $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}]$ units, instead of its conventional plane-conjugated configuration. In ideal status, the angles between the axial directions of paddle wheel units connected by $C_{3}$ symmetric linker should be $\boldsymbol{120}^{\circ}$ , and all the six metal atoms locate in the identical plane. However, in coronene-MOF-1 the angles between paddle wheel axes is actually $86.{09}^{\circ}$ and the six $\overline{{Z}n}^{2+}$ centers define two parallel planes with a distance of 1.59 Å (Figure S7). In contrast to the ideal
