status, huge divergences of these parameters in coronene-MOF-1 ensure that the tpt molecules are in a very tense state. The coincidental location of coronene dimer affords a strong D-A supramolecular interaction with tpt molecules and subsequently stabilizes the trigonal anti-prism cage and the whole structure.
To verify the role of coronene and the related D-A interactions in the assembly of coronene-MOF-1, coronene-absent control experiment was carried out. Eventually, only a $^{1,4}$ -ndc-Zn binary coordination network, namely $[Z\mathsf{n}(1,4\mathsf{-n}\mathsf{d}\mathsf{c})(\mathsf{D}\mathsf{M}\mathsf{A}\mathsf{c})]\mathsf{n}$ (1′), was obtained. Compound $\mathbf{1^{\prime}}$ features a $\scriptstyle2\mathsf{D}\ 4^{4}$ sql network, which is omposed of $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ paddle wheel units and $^{1,4}$ -ndc (Figure S9a). Though sql nets and $^{1,4}$ -ndc and $[Z{\mathsf{n}}_{2}(\mathsf{C O O})_{4}]$ are very common for reticular chemistry, compound $\mathbf{1^{\prime}}$ is first reported here. Unlike porous MOF-2,[14] an early sql network consisting of $\{{2}{\mathsf{n}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}]$ nodes and bdc (terephthalic), a similar linker with ,4-ndc, the adjacent coordination layers in $\mathbf{1^{\prime}}$ are parallel with an ABAB staggered arrangement. Accordingly, the DMAc ligands at axial positions exactly occupy the square void of sql network and makes $\mathbf{1^{\prime}}$ imporous (Figure S9b,c).
The results of control experiment suggest that coronene is essential for the construction of coronene-MOF-1. In consideration of this structure, it could be deduced that coronene exhibits strong D-A interaction with tpt in the assembling process and then afford the tetrameric aromatic D-A stacks. The closed rigonal anti-prism geometry makes sure that the coronene dimer cannot get in after the completion of this coordination cage, and therefore the formation of this tetrameric D-A stacks and coordination cage must be occurred synchronously. More significantly, the D-A interaction within coronene-tpt and coordination assembling are interrelated closely. In detail, the state of dimeric coronene is determined by the height of triangle anti-prism coordination cage, which is defined by the coordination onformation of 1,4-ndc. The distance between two tpt ligands in the moiety fit the distance of D-A and one π-π interactions between the organic components well. Correspondingly, the coronene-free coronene-MOF-1 framework cannot be built because of the huge tension of bending tpt, which has been proved by the coronene-absent control experiment. The coronene dimer exactly stabilizes the unfilled coordination cage and the integrated coordination entities in turn. Therefore, the assembling of coronene-MOF-1 could be clearly attributed to the synergistic of supramolecular D-A, within coronene-tpt system, and the coordination interactions.
To further explore the generality of this synergistically directed assembly strategy, related linear dicarboxylic acids were introduced to verify the effect of coronene-tpt D-A interaction in other systems. As a result, three more coronene-tpt stacks based products, coronene-MOF-2-4, have been obtained with 2-Br-bdc, 2,6-ndc, and abdc, respectively (Figure 2a). Since 2-Br-bdc features quite similar length and preferential vertical conformation of carboxylic groups with 1,4-ndc,[15] coronene-MOF-2 is isostructural with coronene-MOF-1 and contains the same tetrameric tpt-coronene-tpt-coronene stacks and solid trigonal anti-prism supramolecular cages (Figure 2b, S19, and Table 1, S1). In contrast, 2,6-ndc and abdc reveal planer conformation for their intrinsic conjugacy compared with that of $^{1,4}$ -ndc and 2-Br-bdc, and therefore coronene-MOF-3 and -4 present different structure from those of coronene-MOF-1 and -2. Both coronene-MOF-3 and -4 reveal similar waved $4^{4}$ layered structures, consisting of tetrahedrally-coordinated $[Z\mathsf{n N}_{2}0_{2}]$ , linear linkers, and bidentate-bridging tpt (Figure S10a, and S11a). Such layered coordination networks adopt an antiparallel arrangement with no obvious interlayer interactions (Figure $\mathsf{S10b},\mathsf{c},$ and S11b,c). Meanwhile, the uncoordinated pyridyl rings of tpt point into the free space of adjacent below/above layered network with each other, and the residual free space is occupied by coronene. It is notable that coronene presents dimeric state and feature tetrameric tpt-coronene-coronene-tpt stacks in coronene-MOF-3, similar with those in coronene-MOF-1 and -2. This is determined by the antiparallel arrangement of layered coordination networks and the length of 2,6-ndc (Figure 2c, and S10d-f). Correspondingly, the longer abdc generates extra free space at both ends of tetrameric D-A array and affords a hexameric coronene-tpt-coronene-coronene-tpt-coronene stacks in coronene-MOF-4 (Figure 2d, and S11d-f). Thus, the closed correlations between the states of coronene and coordination assembly (the length of linkers) are also observed in coronene-MOF-3 and -4. Furthermore, the tetrameric and
