The coronene-absent control experiments for coronene-MOF-2-4 are also carried out to illustrate the role of coronene in their assembly processes, and three new compounds, $2^{\prime}-4^{\prime}$ are obtained accordingly. All these compounds reveal different structures from the corresponding coronene-MOF (see SI for detail information). These results clearly demonstrates the significance of the presence of coronene and related D-A supramolecular interaction in the assembly of these coronene-MOFs. Their unique structural characteristics, as well as the closed relationship between the substructures of the coronene containing organic SBUs and coordination assembly (refer to length of linkers), clearly proved that these coronene-MOFs are constructed under the synergetic effect of upramolecular D-A and coordination interactions. Therefore, this synergistically directed assembly strategy is proved to be a feasible and general route to construct novel architectures.
## Physicochemical Stability
Although porous MOFs feature many advantages, the general poor stability inevitably hinders their practical applications, specially for Zn-based species due to their flexible coordination geometry.[16] In consideration of the introduction of additional aromatic D-A interaction into the framework, the coronene-MOFs are expected to show enhanced stability. The stability of porous coronene-MOF-1 and -2 was firstly characterized with TGA, which reveals that both compounds remain stable crystalline phase up to about $300^{\circ}\mathsf C,$ and the first weight loss can be ascribed to the removal of solvent guests (Figure S15, S19). In order to examine the stability under extreme conditions, both samples were immersed in diverse organic solvents, the boiling water, and solution with a broad pH range (3 to 11). The measured PXRD patterns show that the crystalline integrity of both coronene-MOF-1 and -2 can be retained well in these conditions igure S16,17). It should be pointed out that most MOFs are ${\mathsf{H}}_{2}{\mathsf{O}}$ instable except those classical structures, mainly involving high-valent metals ions.[17] Therefore, we assume the unusual igh physicochemical stability of coronene-MOF-1/-2 should be closely related to their special internal structural characteristics.
## Adsorption and Separation
On the basis of the stable porous frameworks of oronene-MOF-1 and -2, gas sorption experiments were performed to evaluate their permanent porosity. Prior to gas sorption analysis, both bulk samples were evacuated after ${\mathsf{C H}}_{2}{\mathsf{C l}}_{2}$ exchange and evacuated at room temperature to generate the activated samples (Figure S18,19). $\mathsf{N}_{2}$ sorption tests were carried out at $77~\mathsf{K}$ and both the activated coronene-MOF- $\cdot1/-2$ exhibit reversible type I sorption isotherms with saturation adsorption amount of 278 and $253~\mathsf{c m}^{3}~\mathsf{g}^{-1}$ at 1 atm, respectively (Figure 3a,d). The BET and Langmuir surface areas for coronene-MOF- $\pmb{1}/\pmb{-2}$ derived from the ${\sf N}_{2}$ adsorption isotherm are 852/777 and $1201/1085~{\mathfrak{m}}^{2}~{\mathfrak{g}}^{-1},$ respectively. The pore-size distribution (PSD) analysis of both compounds by the Horvath-Kawazoe method utilizing $\mathsf{N}_{2}$ adsorption data at $77~\mathsf{K}$ indicate identical narrow distribution of the micro-pores at around $10\mathring{\mathsf{A}}$ .
As known, the separation of light hydrocarbons (C2 and C3) from natural gas (mainly as $C H_{4}^{\prime}$ ) is of crucial importance for the petroleum industry. Both $C_{2}H_{6}$ and $C_{3}H_{8}$ are the basic raw materials for various industrial products. For instance, pyrolysis of $C_{2}H_{6}$ and $C_{3}\mathsf{H}_{8}$ can result in ${\mathsf{C}}_{2}{\mathsf{H}}_{4},$ and the dehydrogenation of $C_{3}H_{8}$ can generate $C_{3}H_{6}$ . Both $C_{2}H_{4}$ and $C_{3}H_{6}$ are very important starting petrochemicals for industrial polymers, and $C_{2}H_{4}$ is the organic product on the largest scale industrially. However, the traditional high-pressure cryogenic distillation process for light hydrocarbons separation is extremely energy-consuming. To overcome this problem, the physical adsorption separation of hydrocarbons by porous materials has been regarded as a more promising technology, and MOFs have revealed remarkable performances in this application field.[4] Therefore, the C1-C3 hydrocarbons adsorption and separation performances of coronene-MOF-1 and -2 have been extensively investigated.
