## Conclusions
In summary, a new synergistically directed assembly strategy based on aromatic D-A and coordination interactions for MOFs has been proposed. Based on the strategy, a typical coronene-tpt D-A system is introduced into several coordination systems. The coronene-MOF-1-4 feature distinct coronene-tpt stacks as organic SBUs, resulting in unique structures. The systematic structural tigation of coronene-absent products $\pmb{1^{\prime}-4^{\prime}}$ based on control experiments illustrate the significance of coronene and related D-A interaction in the assembly of coronene-MOFs. Furthermore, the substructures of the coronene containing organic SBUs in different coronene-MOFs are obviously affected by the coordination configuration of the corresponding ligands, indicating the closely relationship between the aromatic D-A and coordination interactions in these systems. In addition to the tuning of structure, the presence of D-A interaction in these particular states also stabilized their whole coordination architectures. All these results prove that this strategy towards romatic D-A stacks based architectures is an effective and general route, which could be instructive for related research. Moreover, the porous coronene-MOF-1 and -2 exhibit high physicochemical stability especially ${\mathsf{H}}_{2}{\mathsf{O}}$ stability as well as moderate surface area and adsorption selectivity of $C_{3}H_{8}/C H_{4}$ and $C2/C H_{4}$ . Further investigation involving this D-A pair and other
coordination interactions are underway in our lab.
## Experimental
Materials and Methods: All the starting reagents and solvents were obtained commercially and used as received. The organic ligand 2,4,6-tri(4-pyridyl)-1,3,5-trizine (tpt) that was prepared according to the literature method.[20] UV−vis spectra were recorded by a SHIMADZU UV-3600 spectrophotometer. Powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) patterns were recorded on a Rigaku D/Max-2500 diffractometer at $40~\mathsf{k V}$ and $100~\mathsf{m A}$ for a Cu-target tube and a graphite monochromator. The powder samples were prepared by crushing the single crystals and the intensity data were taken in the step-scan mode with a scan rate of $10\ \%\sin$ and a step size of $0.02^{\circ}$ . Simulation of the PXRD patterns was performed by diffraction-crystal module of the Mercury program with the single-crystal data. Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) experiments were carried out on a Rigaku standard TG-DTA analyzer under air with a heating rate of $\mathsf{\bar{10}^{\circ}C\mathsf{m i n}^{-1}}$ from room temperature to $800^{\circ}\mathsf{C},$ using an empty ${\mathsf{A l}}_{2}{\mathsf{O}}_{3}$ crucible as reference.
Gas Sorption Measurements: Gas adsorption measurements were carried out using a Micrometrics ASAP 2020 M volumetric gas adsorption analyzer. UHP-grade gases were used in measurements. Before the measurement, the synthesized coronene-MOF-1 and -2 were soaked in anhydrous ${\mathsf{C H}}_{2}{\mathsf{C l}}_{2}$ for 5 days to remove original solvents in channels and then filtrated, and the activation of the ${\mathsf{C H}}_{2}{\mathsf{C l}}_{2}$ -exchanged samples at room temperature under high vacuum (less than ${10}^{-5}$ Torr) for $24\ h$ led to the formation of activated samples. Over $100~\mathsf{m g}$ of both desolvated samples were used for the entire sorption measurements. The ${\sf N}_{2}$ sorption isotherm measurements were proceeded at $77~\mathsf{K}$ in a liquid-nitrogen bath. The $\mathsf{C H}_{4},\mathsf C_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2},\mathsf C_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4},$ ${\mathsf C}_{2}{\mathsf H}_{6},$ and $C_{3}\mathsf{H}_{8}$ sorption isotherm measurements were carried out at 273 and $298\mathsf{K},$ respectively.
Crystallography: All diffraction data were collected on a Rigaku SCX-mini diffractometer at $100~\mathsf{K}$ with $c_{u-K\alpha}$ radiation ( $\lambda=$ $1.54178\mathring{\mathsf{A}})$ by $\omega$ scan mode. The structures were solved by direct methods using the SHELXS program of the SHELXTL package and refined with SHELXL.[21] The disordered solvent molecules of coronene-MOF-1, coronene-MOF-2, $\pmb{2}^{\prime}$ and $\mathbf{3^{\prime}}$ was removed by SQUEEZE as implemented in PLATON and the results were appended in the CIF files.[13]
Synthesis of coronene-MOF-1: A mixture of $Z n(N O_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6H_{2}O$ (29.7 mg, 0.10 mmol), tpt $\cdot10.4~\mathrm{mg},0.033~\mathrm{mmol})$ , 1,4-ndc (21.6 mg, $0.10~\mathsf{m m o l})$ , coronene $(10~\mathrm{~mg},~0.033~\mathrm{~mmol})$ and DMAc $(N,N-$ -dimethylacetamide, $3m L$ ) was sealed into a $20~\mathsf{m L}$ glass vial, which was heated at $120^{\circ}{\mathsf C}$ for $24\ h$ in an oven. After cooling to room temperature, red rhombic crystals were collected and washed three times with $5\mathsf{m L}$ fresh DMAc.
Synthesis of coronene-MOF-2: A mixture of $Z n(N O_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6H_{2}O$ $(29.7~\mathrm{mg},0.10~\mathrm{mmol})$ , tpt $(10.4~\mathrm{mg},0.033~\mathrm{mmol})$ , 2-Br-bdc (24.5 mg, $0.10~\mathrm{\mmol}_{.}$ ), coronene $(10~\mathrm{~mg},~0.033~\mathrm{~mmol})$ and DMF $(N,N$ -dimethylformamide $3m L$ ) was sealed into a $20~\mathsf{m L}$ glass vial, which was heated at $120^{\circ}\mathsf C$ for $24\ h$ in an oven. After cooling to room temperature, red rhombic crystals were collected and washed three times with $5\mathsf{m L}$ fresh DMF.
